{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article","id":1404587,"title":"WtA - Earthblood: Gameplay article","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-25T07:36:41-07:00","id":1404587,"title":"WtA - Earthblood: Gameplay article","content":"So, I found this article about the upcoming Werewolf: The Apocalypse - Earthblood game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.cbr.com/werewolf-the-apocalypse-earthblood-gameplay-analysis/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.cbrimages.com/assets/images/cbr-logo-full-colored-light.svg?v=3.8\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.cbr.com/werewolf-the-apocalypse-earthblood-gameplay-analysis/\" target=\"_blank\"> CBR </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.cbr.com/werewolf-the-apocalypse-earthblood-gameplay-analysis/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.cbr.com/werewolf-the-apocalypse-earthblood-gameplay-analysis/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I must admit I wasn't really interessed until now but from the description it sounds like the game might be better than expected. Seems like tyhey scrapped the Glabro and Hispo forms though and while I get those might not be &quot;different enough&quot; to warrant inclusion I still feel like they could have helped underline how different WtA is from the usual werewolf fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T17:09:32-07:00","id":1407400,"title":"","content":"There's a mention of two &quot;stances&quot; used in combat, but I don't know what that means. My literal interpretation is that they're ways to position your legs and arms. Maybe one is on all fours, analagous to Hispo? But in frenzy the PC will be in both stances simultaneously, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:22:53-08:00","id":1428376,"title":"","content":"Live play footage is out. Such a baby crinos form <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:44:32-08:00","id":1428378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428376#post1428376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Live play footage is out. Such a baby crinos form<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/28HvGmg-Jqg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Omg, its so tiny. I guess they did not want to make combat look AS unbalanced as it does on TT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T14:16:01-08:00","id":1428389,"title":"","content":"pretty sure the war form just looks little cause of the camera. You can tell that it is a few feet taller then the humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T15:33:28-08:00","id":1428402,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the proportions of Crinos look fine at the scale of the camera.<br /> <br /> What bothers me more is the shifting. It looks more like druid rapid spellcasting than a werewolf shifting forms. I get not wanting to have to spend a few seconds (even 2 every time can drag in video games) on changing animations, but a little flourish of energy and instant homid to lupus or back feels very off.<br /> <br /> Something more visceral is sorely lacking. It also could have added some tactical depth if it was harder to shift without breaking stealth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T15:45:59-08:00","id":1428405,"title":"","content":"Vials that increase Rage?<br /> <br /> I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> on the optics of the shifting process.<br /> <br /> But, from what the trailer showed it is an action game for the most past, so there is a huge amount of killing guards, fomori and so on, but really not a lot of other WtA specific elements.<br /> Gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T15:46:14-08:00","id":1428406,"title":"","content":"Damn, this game looks MUCH more better and finished than Bloodlines 2. If only it were for PC. <br /> <br /> Also I agree the size is a little iffy, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar15685_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"15685\" data-vbnamecard=\"15685\">Up-to-Eleven</a> mentions it could just be camera perspective. I do hope that the size gets increased by a few increments, but that seems unlikely. Also the changing does seem fast, but don't you just need Rage to turn instantly? Also Shifting from a tabletop standpoint itself only needs Stamina + Primal-Urge itself right? A Turn in the Storyteller system (besides if you're doing an action that spans multiple turns) is about 3 to 5 seconds right?<br /> <br /> The Shifting in this game actually looks accurate to me. Its just that the size seems off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T16:28:46-08:00","id":1428407,"title":"","content":"If you look at it, human guards are coming up to the Crinos form's shoulders. That's pretty much on point size-wise. The Crinos form can pick up a lab-coat wearing guy, drag them around, and toss them without it looking unreasonable.<br /> <br /> The speed of shifting isn't really the main issue. In the TT rules you can spend 1 rage to reflexively shift, or roll as an instant action to do it in a few seconds (though it takes more than one success), and shifting to your Breed form is already reflexive. There's a Merit that lets you shift to any form reflexively.<br /> <br /> The thing is, regardless of speed, Garou in the TT rules have to shift through all their forms. When you shift from Homid to Lupus, you have to transition through Glabro, Crinos, and Hispo on the way. This means shifting while stealthy is difficult because for a brief moment, you're a giant man-wolf-monster. Shifting in enclosed spaces is also impossible without causing a ruckus and/or scenery destruction. It's also a physical process so bones move around, flesh grows and shrink, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:20:01-08:00","id":1428409,"title":"","content":"Vials that replenish Rage aren't conceptually terrible, it's just that they would be talens in the TT game. This is starting to sound like it is to W:tA as Mechassault is to BattleTech.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428407#post1428407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at it, human guards are coming up to the Crinos form's shoulders. That's pretty much on point size-wise. The Crinos form can pick up a lab-coat wearing guy, drag them around, and toss them without it looking unreasonable.<br /> <br /> The speed of shifting isn't really the main issue. In the TT rules you can spend 1 rage to reflexively shift, or roll as an instant action to do it in a few seconds (though it takes more than one success), and shifting to your Breed form is already reflexive. There's a Merit that lets you shift to any form reflexively.<br /> <br /> The thing is, regardless of speed, Garou in the TT rules have to shift through all their forms. When you shift from Homid to Lupus, you have to transition through Glabro, Crinos, and Hispo on the way. This means shifting while stealthy is difficult because for a brief moment, you're a giant man-wolf-monster. Shifting in enclosed spaces is also impossible without causing a ruckus and/or scenery destruction. It's also a physical process so bones move around, flesh grows and shrink, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the height boost of Crinos and <a href=\"https://www.mrinitialman.com/OddsEnds/Sizes/sizes.html\" target=\"_blank\">this height comparison tool for art</a>, they should be coming up to about the MC's midsection, not his shoulders.<br /> <br /> When you roll, you can bypass forms. Five successes gets you across the spectrum in one turn, which is likely not going to register to human saccades; you'd have to break down individual frames of animation to catch it. This is somewhat supported by the books, as one of the slang terms for werewolves and presumably other werebeasts that Imbued use is flickers, because they can abruptly change into a different form without the human eye registering what happened in between. Slow shifting is for the newly-changed, and if the MC passed that threshold a long time ago, it's going to be on the easier side to elide the other forms. That said, I would go for understated special effects, not glowing energy. Briefly shading and then re-illuminating, at the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:28:33-08:00","id":1428412,"title":"","content":"Yeah I remember from a panel in an old &quot;World of Darkness: Combat&quot; book, there was a page where a Garou was hit with a bat in human form by some gangster. Then he instantly changed right before the gangster's eyes.<br /> <br /> Also newly-changed having trouble changing instantly makes sense, because Tabletop wise either their Stamina or Primal-Urge stats would be low. More advanced or experienced Shape-Changers would be much more faster and change instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-15-2020, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:33:44-08:00","id":1428414,"title":"","content":"Wait, is it not going to be on PC at all? Like, I know that vid said PS4/5 gameplay, but I had hoped that the game would also be on PC...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428405#post1428405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vials that increase Rage?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We have those irl, it's called booze.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T17:56:33-08:00","id":1428416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428409#post1428409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the height boost of Crinos and <a href=\"https://www.mrinitialman.com/OddsEnds/Sizes/sizes.html\" target=\"_blank\">this height comparison tool for art</a>, they should be coming up to about the MC's midsection, not his shoulders.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he was standing perfectly upright? OK (though Crinos shapes and Homid shapes aren't the same). But since he's generally slouching as Crinos is usually drawn with how top heavy they are, that easily accounts for the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you roll, you can bypass forms. </div> </div> </div>You don't bypass forms, you just get through them faster. Maybe fast enough someone doesn't notice, maybe not. The point is that the TT game presents this as a physical rearrangement, not a poof of magic, and that things like running around in Lupus to get up behind someone and then shifting to Homid to stealth kill them, and then shifting back to Lupus, should have a risk of someone noticing (or not rolling well that time).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Also consider that even with 10 dice and a specialty, you'd fail to shift fully from Homid to lupus in one roll ~1/4 of the of time and end up in Hispo for a moment. There's no evidence of that kind of risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-14-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T21:23:57-08:00","id":1428433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428416#post1428416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he was standing perfectly upright? OK (though Crinos shapes and Homid shapes aren't the same). But since he's generally slouching as Crinos is usually drawn with how top heavy they are, that easily accounts for the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>What human accordingly stands fully upright when confronted with the Delirium? They should rightly be shifting about on their feet, nervous as shit at a bare minimum (sometimes literally), and cowering on the verge of running the hell away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't bypass forms, you just get through them faster. </div> </div> </div>Potato, pot<span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u0250</span></span></span>to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe fast enough someone doesn't notice, maybe not. The point is that the TT game presents this as a physical rearrangement, not a poof of magic, and that things like running around in Lupus to get up behind someone and then shifting to Homid to stealth kill them, and then shifting back to Lupus, should have a risk of someone noticing (or not rolling well that time). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm with you on not liking the poof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also consider that even with 10 dice and a specialty, you'd fail to shift fully from Homid to lupus in one roll ~1/4 of the of time and end up in Hispo for a moment. There's no evidence of that kind of risk. </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting might have been a bit too fraught in TT for its own good. Also, if he's Fianna, he might have a Gift to help, since in W20, they get that as in-tribe (and that it exists at all is probably an indicator that someone else thought that shapeshifting might have needed a shot in the arm, too). Failing that, there's the Metamorph merit. Or there could have been assumptions from the official GURPS conversion from way back when (which I only mention because it was technically official).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-15-2020, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T23:33:17-08:00","id":1428438,"title":"","content":"I mean, I am glad that the crinos has a tail, has fur, is actually generally accessible and that lupus form wasn't forgotten.<br /> <br /> It is still an action game, there are certain things that will have to go to make the game work for non-WtA players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T00:37:31-08:00","id":1428442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428433#post1428433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What human accordingly stands fully upright when confronted with the Delirium?</div> </div> </div> </div>The video shows someone ducking and not coming up to the MC's knees in Crinos It's also fairly safe to assume that the game is going to make mooks fomori (the video has two that burst into monsters when they get taken down the first time) or using Pentex drugs that negate the Delerium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Potato, pot\u0250to. </div> </div> </div>Except really not in a this sort of game. If shifting between Homid and Lupus and you have to consider the space you'll take up even for a fraction of a second in Crinos, that's a major deal in a stealth-action game. Knocking stuff over, pinging sensors, being forced to deal with something in Lupus because there isn't room to shift, etc. As I said before, the weird thing is that not only does it go against the lore of WtA, it removes easy ways for level designers to add challenge to the game by putting in points where you have to use shifting more strategically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shapeshifting might have been a bit too fraught in TT for its own good. </div> </div> </div>Eh? It's never been IME. Most of the time it's either combat and you'll use Rage, or out of combat and you'll take a few turns to be in the form you want to be in since it's unlikely to change as frequently. The few times where players are going to feel pressure to roll, but not just spend Rage, are pretty specific, and the &quot;fraught&quot; part is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Even if he has any of the ways to boost his shifting, it doesn't address the larger concern. I was just pointing out that high level PC doesn't equate to automatic shifting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428438#post1428438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is still an action game, there are certain things that will have to go to make the game work for non-WtA players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is arguing against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T01:35:42-08:00","id":1428445,"title":"","content":"I'll add this to the list of extremely underwhelming WoD video games that we've accumulated over the years and especiallly recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:20:02-08:00","id":1428475,"title":"","content":"There isn't a table top source for a talen that replenishes Rage and if find it thematically unsatisfactory.<br /> <br /> The game is for PC too, and can also already be bought, for example in the epic game store.<br /> <br /> So far, we have only seen action sequences, with the PC in a map where certain objectives are to be reached. No interaction with allies or stuff like that was shown so far, that is a pity, for now I fear it will only be an fighting game where you clear level after level. So, it might be rather forgettable.<br /> <br /> What made Bloodlines I memorable, were the NPC, cut scenes and overall story and gameplay, besides the fighting. Heck, the whole vacant haunted Hotel was great, and it didn't have much fighting in it.<br /> What I saw from the trailer, the fights seemed quite sterile, in a way like the old ONI game, less than the newer Doom or Resident Evil, with a really great mood and atmosphere. I hope the game will have elements like this.<br /> <br /> Running through a forest to beat the a fomori strike team to the caern habitat area, the penumbra of a cemetery or waste dump site. And such stuff - although I hate minigames in most cases....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 12-15-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T06:20:58-08:00","id":1428592,"title":"","content":"I'm also a little anoyed by Rage regening from hitting enemies rather then when *you* take damage like the tabletop but that's a minor quible that I am very happy to sacrifice in the name of good game mechanincs.<br /> <br /> Of course if the game is bad then that will be an extra nitpick for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T06:32:42-08:00","id":1428594,"title":"","content":"I find a bit worrying that the &quot;penumbral vision&quot; seems to be your typical &quot;scan skill&quot; to check where enemies are and such. Instead of showing...well...the spirit world (showing immaterial spirits, and other ephemeral stuff). <i>Right now </i>it doesn't seem like the spiritual aspects of being a werewolf are getting much love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T07:18:12-08:00","id":1428597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428592#post1428592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a little anoyed by Rage regening from hitting enemies rather then when *you* take damage like the tabletop but that's a minor quible that I am very happy to sacrifice in the name of good game mechanincs.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\">No, you don't get Rage from being hit. A lot of people say that, and a lot of them are wrong. You get a free Frenzy Check for being wounded.<br /> <br /> Regaining Rage (aside from Gifts/Rites/Fetishes and stuff) is limited to:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Moon:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> The first time a werewolf sees the moon at night, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the Beast inside stirs, and Rage floods back into her.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Botch:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> If the Storyteller approves, a werewolf might receive a </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Rage point after a botched a roll.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Humiliation:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Rage will also come rushing back if anything a </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Garou does proves particularly humiliating.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Confrontation:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Again at the Storyteller\u2019s approval, a character </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">could receive a Rage point at the beginning of a tense situation, in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">the moments right before combat starts. This gain accounts for the </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">anticipation and hackle-raising that happens just as tempers start to flare.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">New Stories:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> When a new story begins, each player should </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">roll a die to determine how many Rage points he possesses currently.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:51:53-08:00","id":1428657,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Fomori that can shapeshift are a bit of a luxury. Also, the ones that go into combat with Garou are usually a bit over the top in their physical enhancements. As for Garou shapeshifting, Form Mastery still exists as of W20, and one could easily imagine more Gifts in the same wheelhouse. If you really need a TT explanation for so much quick shapeshifting, Metamorph also exists (though for returning to Homid from Lupus, that's easy for a homid-born character). The physical space requirements are going to be a problem, but sensors, I'm not so sure. I don't know if there were any rulings made over whether or not your footprints changed at five successes, but if they don't, observational devices would probably have a hard time registering what happened. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428475#post1428475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a table top source for a talen that replenishes Rage and if find it thematically unsatisfactory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia's Best from the old Fianna tribebook. It was from a different time, perhaps, but then, even it required a roll to gain its benefits (full recovery of Rage and Willpower) instead of becoming less than 100%, shall we say.<br /> <br /> But in any case, this probably isn't that, so, again, the Mechassault of Werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T14:28:46-08:00","id":1428665,"title":"","content":"Imagine how much more overpowered Garou would be if they actually gained more Rage with every hit they get. lmao.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T15:19:58-08:00","id":1428668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428657#post1428657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Fomori that can shapeshift are a bit of a luxury. Also, the ones that go into combat with Garou are usually a bit over the top in their physical enhancements.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point was just that at a Pentex facility, there's going to be a lot of Delirium immune/resistant characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Garou shapeshifting, Form Mastery still exists as of W20, and one could easily imagine more Gifts in the same wheelhouse. If you really need a TT explanation for so much quick shapeshifting, Metamorph also exists (though for returning to Homid from Lupus, that's easy for a homid-born character). </div> </div> </div>You know, I pointed out a lot of this stuff from the get go, right? Pointing out all the ways the Garou can boost shapeshifting with the right Gifts/Merits/etc. just feels like pointless and inaccurate nitpicking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The physical space requirements are going to be a problem, but sensors, I'm not so sure. I don't know if there were any rulings made over whether or not your footprints changed at five successes, but if they don't, observational devices would probably have a hard time registering what happened. </div> </div> </div>What do footprints have to do with things like infrared security sensors noticing a giant heat signature?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428665#post1428665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine how much more overpowered Garou would be if they actually gained more Rage with every hit they get. lmao.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot. Though they've said from the get go that this game is going to have a Frenzy mechanic where you build up Rage at the risk of going berserk; which tempers things a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T15:27:30-08:00","id":1428670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428665#post1428665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine how much more overpowered Garou would be if they actually gained more Rage with every hit they get. lmao.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if WW5e does take mechanics from V5, then I could imagine that there was an increase in, lets say, Frenzy each time you activate Rage driven Gifts, for example.<br /> <br /> Besides that, there are &quot;Silver Claws&quot;. Each round one Rage regain. That is pretty cool, but really only good if you can prepare for a fight, since the activation requires Gnosis, iirc, and that would disallow Rage spending, so if you get surprised, you better spend a whole lot of Rage on instant shapeshifting and multiple actions. Because, Rage actions are broken and will always be the thing that makes Garou overpowered. I'm very glad how V20DA redesigned Celerity and how V5 removed the multiple actions element all together. I hope WW5e goes the same route.<br /> Despite the imo unnecessary changes to the Setting, I liked some of the mechanics of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T15:40:19-08:00","id":1428672,"title":"","content":"Damn, I hope all the &quot;new&quot; mechanics just stay in V5 and I also hope Werewolf doesn't take ANY go down any routes of V5- but this is wishful thinking at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T01:47:26-08:00","id":1428722,"title":"","content":"Well, some mechanics in Werewolf are a bit undesirable, in my opinion. So, while I would really like the setting to stay more or less the way revised was (and not W20), I would certainly hope for a greater mechanics overhaul as the V20/W20 was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T20:51:41-08:00","id":1429290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archmage Joda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428414#post1428414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is it not going to be on PC at all? Like, I know that vid said PS4/5 gameplay, but I had hoped that the game would also be on PC...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have those irl, it's called booze.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it\u2019s going to be on PC, but it is an epic store exclusive if that matters to you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T23:42:46-08:00","id":1429303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1429290#post1429290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it\u2019s going to be on PC, but it is an epic store exclusive if that matters to you</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh. I didn't know it was going to be on PC.. but epic store exclusive sounds shady, so no buy from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T01:34:42-08:00","id":1429311,"title":"","content":"There are other vendors who sell coupons for epic store. In the PC games market, there are lots of games that are exclusive to one store to bait customers.<br /> <br /> And Epic, despite starting out 30 years ago as a one person company is now nearing US$17 billion worth. So, I think you are safe there, that they will deliver.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T16:36:13-08:00","id":1429434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1404587-wta-earthblood-gameplay-article?p=1428594#post1428594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find a bit worrying that the &quot;penumbral vision&quot; seems to be your typical &quot;scan skill&quot; to check where enemies are and such. Instead of showing...well...the spirit world (showing immaterial spirits, and other ephemeral stuff). <i>Right now </i>it doesn't seem like the spiritual aspects of being a werewolf are getting much love.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is essentially my exact feeling on the game, however, it goes beyond being disappointed with the importing Batman's &quot;Detective Vision,&quot; filing off the serial numbers and calling it &quot;penumbral vision.&quot; All of the gameplay looks generic--stuff I've done in a dozen or more other games over the years.<br /> <br /> The &quot;abilities&quot; appear to let you perform canned claw strike sequences of varying sizes and speeds, a ground slam, you have a crossbow for deactivating electronics (instead of, gee I dunno, Jam Technology, which is a low-rank Homid Gift). The different forms look pretty whatever--there is functionally no difference between turning into a wolf to move more stealthily, and hitting a button to crouch (and move more stealthily.) The fact that you go into Crinos to fight is <i>fine</i> I guess. What I would have liked to have seen would have been for there to be more than one form that's good for whatever task--if there's just not question about which form I'm going to use to do any given sort of task, there's nothing tactical or special about that; they've basically just made a game like any other, but made it so you gotta hit a particular button before you get into a fight/try to sneak around/use a computer. I'll reserve completely judgment about how the Umbra is utilized because there's not a whole lot of gameplay footage available, and for all I know there will be a Soul Reaver-like mechanics where you can move back and forth at will to access things or rooms via one world that are blocked off or otherwise inaccessible in the other. I'm not holding my breath though. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}